WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.400
Adult Swim's runaway sensation wrapped up
its third season in October 2017, and fans

00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.280
have been waiting patiently for a fourth season
ever since.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:13.570
Fortunately, a brand new batch of Rick and
Morty episodes is finally in production and

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:14.920
on its way to television.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:16.980
Here's everything we know so far.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:22.060
For patient Rick and Morty fans, the long
wait for new multigenerational universe-hopping

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.820
adventures is nearly over.

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:29.740
In May 2019, Adult Swim's parent company WarnerMedia
held its "upfront" presentation in New York.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:34.120
Fans hoped against hope that there'd be some
good news about the long-awaited fourth season

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.280
of Rick and Morty, and Warner delivered, announcing
that Rick and Morty would return at the end

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:39.280
of the year.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:46.360
"Everybody, uh...Rick and Morty is back, brand
new Season 4, in November 2019 this year.

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.400
We're gonna do it this year."

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:50.620
But when, exactly, in November 2019?

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:55.339
Warner didn't say, only that the series would
show up sometime in the weeks or days before

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.780
or after Thanksgiving.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:01.880
With some exceptions, most American television
shows don't take too long of a break between

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.680
seasons.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:07.400
Most broadcast network shows run from September
to May, while cable channels or streaming

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.920
services might drop a 13-episode season of
a series in the spring, and then return with

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.900
another 13 about a year later.

00:01:13.900 --> 00:01:18.500
But the wait between seasons three and four
of Rick and Morty has been comically, frustratingly

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:19.500
long.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:24.700
"See ya for season 4 in like, a really long
time.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.300
I might even have a big white Santa Claus
beard."

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.780
Delays are nothing new with Rick and Morty.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.460
About 15 months passed between the end of
season one and the beginning of season two,

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:39.360
and there was a good year and a half between
season two and the beginning of season three.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:44.140
The two-year wait for season four, however,
is easily the longest in series history.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:48.720
Series co-creators Justin Roiland and Dan
Harmon have commented on the sometimes lengthy

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.580
wait for Adult Swim to order new episodes,
and the complex process of negotiating for

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:57.620
a budget large enough to give the show, quote,
"the attention it deserves."

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.620
In March 2018, Harmon guested on Kevin Smith
and Scott Mosier's SModcast.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:07.540
At the time neither he nor Roiland were actively
working on creating more Rick and Morty episodes.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:11.380
He explained that the reason was simple enough:
business problems, saying,

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:22.340
But it all worked out in the end: two months
later, Adult Swim ordered a whopping 70 new

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.400
episodes of Rick and Morty.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.760
That means Roiland and Harmon are contractually
obligated to churn out Rick and Morty for

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.780
years to come.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:30.780
"Season, nine more seasons, Morty.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.400
Nine more seasons until I get that dipping
Szechuan sauce."

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.100
"What is that?!"

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:35.100
"For 97 more years, Morty."

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.260
Previous seasons have run for 10 or 11 episodes.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:43.240
At one point during the production of season
three, Harmon had hoped to produce 14 episodes,

00:02:43.250 --> 00:02:45.010
but the schedule forced a cutback.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.540
In late 2017, he told Entertainment Weekly
that he'd like to give that idea another try.

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:55.060
Rick and Morty's creative team doesn't have
too hard of a time keeping its voice cast

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:56.160
under contract.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.060
That's because the two main characters are
voiced by Justin Roiland, who is also the

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:02.900
show's co-creator and primary creative force.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:05.360
"Oh Morty, help me Morty.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.500
Help me Rick.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.780
Help me Rick.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.300
Perfect."

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.040
Sarah Chalke, who has voiced Beth Smith for
the show's entire run, confirmed to Entertainment

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.720
Tonight Canada in April 2019 that she's coming
back, too.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:22.260
There will also be some big names joining
the small club of Rick and Morty guest voices,

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:25.760
which includes John Oliver, Christina Hendricks,
and Danny Trejo.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.840
Sam Neill is also apparently making a voice
contribution.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:31.340
On Halloween 2018, Neill tweeted:

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:39.140
Finally, in a May 2019 interview with HollywoodLife,
Roiland broke the news that Paul Giamatti

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:41.900
would soon be recording lines for an upcoming
episode.

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:42.940
"And you know what?

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.520
God bless you, Paul Giamatti.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:49.320
You're a hero, an angel, no sorry go ahead."

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:54.340
The upcoming fourth season of Rick and Morty
is still in production, as Roiland, Harmon

00:03:54.340 --> 00:04:00.180
and crew barrel into the future and a promised
premiere date of sometime in November 2019.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:05.460
That's only a few months away, but as of July
2019 there's no official Rick and Morty trailer

00:04:05.460 --> 00:04:06.360
available.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.220
However, Adult Swim has put out several 15-second
promo commercials for the upcoming season.

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.099
"What the hell is a promo commercial anyway?"

00:04:13.099 --> 00:04:14.360
"It's a disposable advertisement.

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.360
It's meaningless.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.160
It doesn't matter."

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:21.500
The first was a trippy montage that showed
Rick devouring Morty in various animal forms.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:25.820
The second, released on the Rick and Morty
Twitter account, is similarly trippy, but

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.400
with a 4th of July theme.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.060
Happy Birthday, America!

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.060
"Notify the president."

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.070
"What do I tell him?

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.100
Tell him the truth.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:35.660
Tell him Rick and Morty just blew off America."

00:04:35.669 --> 00:04:40.370
Anyone who watches Adult Swim knows that these
kinds of promos are a common form of "station

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:45.040
ID" designed to show off their lineup without
any direct connection to episode content.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.860
But it does serve as a taste of new footage
for fans hungry to know about the creative

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.780
headspace in which the Rick and Morty team
are currently operating.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.480
You know, besides the usual.

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:55.240
"I hafta need another shot.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.240
Just kidding.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:57.240
Joking.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:59.460
This is gonna be the f---ing whiz kid take.

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:00.880
I'm a whiz kid."

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.560
What will actually happen in season four?

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:07.200
Show creators Justin Roiland and Dan Harmon
are keeping quiet.

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:12.320
In a 2019 interview with HollywoodLife, neither
of them were any help, jokingly riffing on

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.400
Harmon's "story circle" writing process that
forms the basis of every episode.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:21.080
"Oh, Rick is gonna learn a very valuable lesson
and pay a heavy price.

00:05:21.560 --> 00:05:23.480
And Morty too I think at one point."

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.140
"Yeah."

00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.500
Rick and Morty storyboard artist Douglas Olsen
posted some tweets about Evil Morty, eventually

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.500
saying:

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:35.820
Another fan favorite bit could make a return.

00:05:35.820 --> 00:05:41.360
On February 8, 2019, Roiland posted an Instagram
picture from inside a recording booth with

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.880
the caption "Idc3 (maybe)."

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:48.240
The Rick and Morty mastermind might be teasing
a third "Interdimensional Cable" episode.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:49.980
"Hey, what are you doing?"

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:50.980
"A sequel."

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:52.229
"I don't understand."

00:05:52.229 --> 00:05:53.220
"Yeah, me neither."

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.419
Hardcore Rick and Morty fans who want to see
an episode of the show's forthcoming season

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:02.600
a little early may want to drop some cash
on a trip to the 2019 Adult Swim Festival.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:07.960
Like Coachella but with way more weird comedy,
the event takes place on November 15 and 16

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.240
in Los Angeles.

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:13.490
The festival's biggest draw is likely the
screening of a brand new episode from Season

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:14.440
4 of Rick and Morty.

00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:18.640
Organizers haven't said if it's the season
premiere or an installment from later on in

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:23.151
this new batch of episodes, but it is the
first debut of any new Rick and Morty episode

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:24.800
since 2017.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.100
"Rick, no, you can't."

00:06:26.100 --> 00:06:26.600
"Too late, Morty.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:27.600
The hole's opening."

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:28.960
"No, no, Rick, you don't understand…"

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:32.420
"And there's a lot more where that came from,
too."

